  "email": "sofia.rossi@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports Teams camera black screen and others can't hear her. Need account, devices, and usual hours."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "Confirm laptop is online and checking in, and check for camera/mic related warnings while troubleshooting Teams camera and audio issue for Sofia Rossi."
}

{
  "query": "Teams camera black screen microphone others cannot hear",
  "reason": "Confirm the right KB article for Teams camera and audio issue."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry about the trouble on your Teams calls. Please try these steps on your laptop and let us know what happens: 1) In Teams, go to Settings, then Devices, and make sure the correct microphone, speaker, and camera are selected. If you use a headset or docking station, check that it is selected there too. 2) Check that the laptop's physical mute key is off and the camera privacy shutter (if it has one) is open. 3) Close other apps that might be using the camera, such as Zoom or browser tabs with video calls. 4) Fully quit Teams (right-click its taskbar icon and choose Quit), then reopen it. 5) Use Teams' 'Make a test call' option to check your audio. If the camera still shows black or others still can't hear you after these steps, please reply with the name of the laptop you are calling from and whether the problem continues after a restart, and we will escalate it.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-soft-01, Sofia Rossi (user_id 7, Marketing Coordinator, active, not blocked, VPN enabled). Single enrolled device BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11, 54.7% disk free) shows offline with no check-in for 12 days (last check-in 2026-09-29). This may mean she is working on a different machine, or the laptop is powered off or disconnected, so I could not confirm device state or camera detection. Applied KB-025 quick checks via user instructions only; no action tools used. Escalation criteria in KB-025 (persists after restart, or camera not detected by Windows) not yet confirmed. Next steps: confirm which device she is using, then check whether the issue persists after restart. If Windows does not detect the camera, escalate as a hardware fault. Please also look into the 12-day check-in gap on BL-LT-0107.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-025"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
